            <ArticleTitle>Substance abuse issues in cancer pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>183-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It is estimated that 40% to 50% of patients with metastatic disease and 90% of patients with terminal cancer experience unrelieved pain. Furthermore, inadequate treatment of cancer pain is a greater possibility if the patient is a substance abuser. In this paper, we will explore pertinent conceptual and clinical aspects of addiction that can assist in improving the identification and treatment of patients with substance use disorders.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
